    "title": "Where is the men's basketball national championship game? Location for Michigan-UConn",
    "text": "April 6, 2026, 6:01 p.m. ETA 2025-26 men's college basketball season that began with more than 360 teams nationally dreaming of a national championship — some more realistically than others — is now down to one game and two teams.No. 1 seed Michigan and No. 2 seed UConn will square off on Monday, April 6 in the title game of the 2026 NCAA Tournament, with the winner earning a place among some of the greatest teams in the sport's history.The Wolverines, who have rolled to the championship game by winning their five tournament games by an average of 21.6 points, are seeking their first national title since 1989. The Huskies, meanwhile, are looking for their third championship in the past four years, which would further cement their status as the sport's modern-day dynasty.This will all be happening in a place as synonymous with basketball as anywhere in the country.As the leadup to the event begins, here’s what you need to know about the this year’s national championship game, including its location:Where is the men’s national championship game?Location: Lucas Oil Stadium (Indianapolis)The national championship game of the 2026 NCAA men’s basketball tournament will be held at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis, the home of the NFL’s Indianapolis Colts.It will be the fourth time that the 18-year-old stadium has hosted the Final Four. It last did so in 2021, in front of a limited crowd that was watching the event during the COVID-19 pandemic. It will be the ninth time Indianapolis has served as the Final Four host, making it the second-most-common Final Four location, behind only Kansas City, which has had 10 Final Fours (though it hasn't hosted since 1988).National championship game dateDates: April 6Michigan's matchup against UConn in the national championship game will take place on Monday, April 6.National championship start timeStart time: 8:50 p.m. ETThe national championship game between Michigan and UConn is scheduled to tip off at 8:50 p.m. ET.Future Final Four locationsHere's a look at where the Final Four will be in the next five years:2027: Ford Field, Detroit2028: Allegiant Stadium, Las Vegas2029: Lucas Oil Stadium, Indianapolis2030: AT&T Stadium, Arlington, Texas2031: Mercedes-Benz Stadium, AtlantaWhat channel is the national championship game on?TV channel: TBS, truTVStreaming: Sling TVThe national championship game between Michigan and UConn will be broadcast on TBS and truTV. Ian Eagle (play-by-play), Bill Raftery (analyst) and Grant Hill (analyst) will be on the call while Tracy Wolfson will serve as the sideline reporter.Streaming options for the games include Sling TV, which carries TBS and the Turner Sports family of networks.Watch the NCAA basketball championship game live with Sling TVWho’s in the national championship game?No. 1 MichiganNo. 2 UConnThe championship game of the 2026 NCAA Tournament will pit No. 1 seed Michigan against No. 2 seed UConn.",
